      "text": "To find the probability that four fair 6-sided dice will not all show the same number, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of possible outcomes when rolling four dice.\n2. Calculate the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.\n3. Subtract the number of outcomes where all dice show the same number from the total number of outcomes to find the number of outcomes where not all dice show the same number.\n4. Divide this number by the total number of outcomes to find the probability.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of possible outcomes**\n\nEach die has 6 faces, so the total number of outcomes when rolling four dice is:\n\\[ 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 6^4 = 1296 \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number**\n\nThere are 6 possible outcomes where all four dice show the same number (they can all show 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6). So, there are 6 favorable outcomes.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the number of outcomes where not all four dice show the same number**\n\nThe number of outcomes where not all four dice show the same number is:\n\\[ 1296 - 6 = 1290 \\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the probability**\n\nThe probability that not all four dice show the same number is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes:\n\\[ \\frac{1290}{1296} = \\frac{215}{216} \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same number is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{215}{216}} \\]",
